11
00:47:08,571 --> 00:47:14,571
Love & Mercy is a 2014 American biographical drama film directed by Bill Pohlad about the Beach Boys'
co-founder and leader Brian Wilson and his struggles with mental illness during the 1960s and 1980s.

12
00:51:25,714 --> 00:51:31,714
It stars Paul Dano and John Cusack as the young and older Wilson, respectively, with Elizabeth
Banks as his second wife Melinda Ledbetter and Paul Giamatti as his psychologist Dr.

13
00:55:42,857 --> 00:55:48,857
Eugene Landy.

14
01:00:00,000 --> 01:00:06,000
The title comes from Wilson's 1988 song of the same name.

15
01:04:17,142 --> 01:04:23,142
The film alternates between Wilson's production of the album Pet Sounds (1966) and
his treatment under Landy's 24-hour therapy program in the late 1980s.

16
01:08:34,285 --> 01:08:40,285
Wilson called the film "very factual", despite containing
parts that "weren't actually as factual".

17
01:12:51,428 --> 01:12:57,428
He had little involvement with its making, although
Ledbetter was relied upon for the 1980s portions.

18
01:17:08,571 --> 01:17:14,571
The cast and crew maintained that nothing in the film was a "Hollywood"
embellishment and that everything was intended to be as truthful as possible.

19
01:21:25,714 --> 01:21:31,714
Conversely, Landy's son Evan felt that his father was unfairly portrayed.

20
01:25:42,857 --> 01:25:48,857
Some minor inaccuracies were noted by critics, a number of which relate to the
minimal coverage devoted to Wilson's family and collaborators.

21
01:30:00,000 --> 01:30:06,000
Ledbetter said that Landy's treatment of Wilson "was
even worse" than the film portrays.

22
01:34:17,142 --> 01:34:23,142
Love & Mercy premiered at the 2014 Toronto International Film Festival on September 7,
2014 and was released by Lionsgate and Roadside Attractions on June 5, 2015.

23
01:38:34,285 --> 01:38:40,285
It grossed $28.6 million over a $10 million budget and received positive reviews
from critics, with Dano's performance garnering significant praise.

24
01:42:51,428 --> 01:42:57,428
It was nominated for two Golden Globes: Best Supporting Actor – Motion
Picture (Paul Dano) and Best Original Song ("One Kind of Love").

25
01:47:08,571 --> 01:47:14,571
A soundtrack album that includes the original score by
Atticus Ross was released on August 14, 2015.

26
01:51:25,714 --> 01:51:31,714
The film explores themes of rock 'n' roll, musician,
therapist, biography, recording studio.

27
01:55:42,857 --> 01:55:48,857
The tone is emotional.
